    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Parse an interval.</para><para>An interval is specified in one of the following forms, where <ref refid="namespaceN" kindref="compound">N</ref> and M are non-negative integers:</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>&quot;N&quot; is a singleton interval. </para></listitem>
<listitem><para>&quot;N,M&quot; is the min/max form specifying the two inclusive end points. M must not be less than <ref refid="namespaceN" kindref="compound">N</ref>. </para></listitem>
<listitem><para>&quot;N-M&quot; is the begin/end form where M is greater than <ref refid="namespaceN" kindref="compound">N</ref> and not included in the interval. </para></listitem>
<listitem><para>&quot;N+M&quot; is the base/size form where <ref refid="namespaceN" kindref="compound">N</ref> is the minimum value and M is the number of items.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
The integers can be specified in decimal, octal, hexadecimal, or binary using the usual C/C++ syntax. </para>    </detaileddescription>
